# These are parsed by Linux tooling -- the Cloud Build image build, gcloud, and
# systemd on the VM -- so they must stay LF regardless of a Windows checkout's
# core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF Dockerfile puts a trailing \r on every RUN line,
# and a CRLF shell script breaks on its own shebang.
#
# .py is deliberately absent: Python reads either ending, so pinning it would
# only renormalise the whole package for no gain.
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
.dockerignore       text eol=lf
*.yaml              text eol=lf
*.yml               text eol=lf
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.service           text eol=lf
*.timer             text eol=lf
